.TH IAD\-PAGE\-TRANSITION 3 "" "iced-adaptive-design 0.1.0" "iced-adaptive-design Manual"
.SH NAME
page_transition \- Fades content in whenever key changes: the AdwViewStack cross\-fade (200ms, ease\-out\-quad) for switching pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
page_transition(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, key: impl Into<u64>)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Fades \fBcontent\fR in whenever \fBkey\fR changes: the \fBAdwViewStack\fR cross\-fade (200ms, ease\-out\-quad) for switching pages. The page below is not kept, so the new page fades up out of the window background rather than blending with the old one.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B page_transition(content: impl Into<Element<'a, M, Theme>>, key: impl Into<u64>)
.SH PROPERTIES
Builder methods, chained after the constructor.
.TP
.B \&.trigger(t: Trigger)
Which trigger this fade is (default \fBTrigger::PageChange\fR); its \fB[motion]\fR setting, or reduced motion, can turn it off.
.TP
.B \&.scroll_key(key: impl Into<u64>)
Identifies the page for its scroll position, when that differs from the fade's key (a page that is not faded, like the parent page of a collapsed split view, still scrolls on its own). Defaults to the fade's key.
